.Dd October 9, 2026
.Dt DOOR 2
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm door
.Nd multiplexed kernel entry point for Doors IPC
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/types.h
.In sys/door_core.h
.In sys/syscall.h
.In unistd.h
.Ft long
.Fn __syscall "quad_t SYS_door" "long op" "long arg1" "long arg2" "long arg3" "long arg4" "long arg5"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
system call is the native kernel transport used by
.Xr door 3 .
It multiplexes the complete Doors ABI through the selector
.Fa op
and five machine-word operands.
Applications should normally use
.Xr door 3
instead of issuing this system call directly.
.Pp
The ABI version is
.Dv DOOR_ABI_VERSION .
Pointer operands refer to calling-process virtual addresses.
All public request structures contain a version field and reserved fields;
reserved fields must be zero.
.Pp
The selectors are defined in
.In sys/door_core.h :
.Bl -tag -width DOOR_SC_SHM_DESTROY
.It Dv DOOR_SC_CREATE
Create a Door owned by the calling process and return its descriptor.
.It Dv DOOR_SC_REVOKE
Revoke an owned Door and abort pending or active operations.
.It Dv DOOR_SC_INFO
Return owner, generation, attributes, and queue information.
.It Dv DOOR_SC_CALL
Invoke according to endpoint mode (synchronous reply or ONEWAY acceptance) using
.Vt struct door_ioc_call .
.It Dv DOOR_SC_FAST_CALL
Perform the scalar data-only call form.
.It Dv DOOR_SC_EMPTY_CALL
Perform the specialized empty request form.
.It Dv DOOR_SC_ONEWAY
Snapshot and submit a data-only asynchronous request.
.It Dv DOOR_SC_RETURN
Complete and normally receive the next invocation.
Successful NEED_BUFS, REWAIT or EXIT outcomes contain no next request; inspect
.Dv DOOR_RETURN_F_*
flags before using receive outputs.
.It Dv DOOR_SC_FAST_RETURN
Use the scalar data-only return form.
.It Dv DOOR_SC_EMPTY_RETURN
Return an empty reply with the same receive outcome protocol.
.It Dv DOOR_SC_FAST_CALL_MAPPED , Dv DOOR_SC_EMPTY_CALL_MAPPED
Scalar calls permitting AUTO_MAP reply replacement. Decode the full packed
result and, when present, the mapping metadata defined in
.In sys/door_core.h ;
the caller owns the replacement mapping.
.It Dv DOOR_SC_ASYNC_CALL
Submit snapshotted data with a held completion capability and reserved slot.
The server uses normal RETURN; one terminal completion is scheduled.
.It Dv DOOR_SC_ASYNC_CANCEL
Cancel using request and completion capabilities. Cancellation does not stop
an already running server callback.
.It Dv DOOR_SC_CANCEL
Cancel a call owned by the calling process.
.It Dv DOOR_SC_GETPARAM , Dv DOOR_SC_SETPARAM
Read or modify per-Door limits.
.It Dv DOOR_SC_BIND , Dv DOOR_SC_UNBIND
Bind or unbind the calling thread as a server worker.
.It Dv DOOR_SC_WORKER_EXIT
Release a worker binding during thread teardown.
.It Dv DOOR_SC_CRED
Obtain the captured credentials of the current invocation.
.It Dv DOOR_SC_SHM_CREATE , Dv DOOR_SC_SHM_ATTACH
Create or attach a persistent shared-memory region.
.It Dv DOOR_SC_CALL_SHM
Invoke a Door using a validated region, offset, and length tuple.
.It Dv DOOR_SC_SHM_DESTROY
Invalidate a persistent region handle.
.El
.Pp
Descriptors are capabilities.
Jail policy is checked when a capability is acquired. Descriptor Capsicum
rights are checked for each operation, including CALL; per-Door limits remain
in effect.
A successful open or connect pins the selected Door generation; ordinary calls
do not repeat pathname or jail lookup.
.Pp
The system call is present independently of
.Cd "options DOORFS" .
If Door support is not configured, every selector returns
.Er ENOSYS .
.Ss ONEWAY delivery and revoke
Successful ONEWAY submission means acceptance after copied-data capture or
checked SHM reference acquisition, not callback completion.
Under the Door lock the worker commits server-reference lifetime before
unlocking for request export.
Revoke can detach an assigned but uncommitted request; after commitment,
RETURN or worker teardown retains cleanup responsibility even if copyout fails.
The internal asynchronous lifetime flag is also used by native async CALL,
which has correlated kernel completion and a separate result contract.
.Ss Reply MOVE commit
Successful receiver installation commits reply MOVE.
A concurrent endpoint revoke cannot bypass installation acknowledgement or
replace that committed transfer with EBADF while source consumption is pending.
CALL waits until the server consumes the matching source descriptor and
acknowledges MOVE.
Installation failure preserves the source; a later final syscall-argument
copyout fault remains an uncertain-result case.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
On success, the return value depends on the selector.
Creation returns a descriptor; other selectors generally return zero or encode
their documented scalar result in the return registers.
Use the full-width
.Fn __syscall
result as libdoor does; scalar forms pack flags above bit 31, so truncating
the result to int loses output information. The scalar ABI requires the
supported machine-word width; raw callers must follow the architecture ABI.
On failure, -1 is returned and
.Va errno
is set.
.Sh ERRORS
In addition to selector-specific errors,
.Nm
may return:
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EINVAL
The selector, ABI version, flags, reserved fields, pointer/length combination,
or current worker state is invalid.
.It Bq Er EBADF
A descriptor or Door generation is invalid or revoked.
.It Bq Er EFAULT
A supplied userspace range cannot be read or written.
.It Bq Er EACCES
Jail policy or mapping permissions deny capability acquisition.
.It Bq Er ENOTCAPABLE
The descriptor lacks the required Capsicum right.
.It Bq Er EINTR
A cancellable synchronous wait was interrupted.
.It Bq Er ECANCELED
The call was explicitly cancelled.
.It Bq Er ECONNRESET
An assigned worker disappeared without endpoint revocation.
.It Bq Er EPERM
Ownership or publication scope denies the operation.
.It Bq Er EAGAIN
Async context or completion admission is full.
.It Bq Er ENOBUFS
A request violates the per-Door data-size limits.
.It Bq Er ENFILE
A request exceeds the per-Door descriptor limit.
.It Bq Er ENOTSUP
Descriptor transfer or the requested operation is unsupported.
.It Bq Er EMSGSIZE
A reply/receive buffer or async payload bound is exceeded.
.It Bq Er EBUSY
The operation conflicts with an active worker, mapping, reservation, or vfork
state.
.It Bq Er ENOMEM
Kernel memory, VM pages, mappings, or descriptor bookkeeping could not be
allocated.
.It Bq Er ENOSYS
The kernel was built without
.Cd "options DOORFS" .
.El
.Sh CAPABILITY MODE
The system call is permitted in capability mode.
Individual operations require the corresponding
.Dv CAP_DOOR_CALL ,
.Dv CAP_DOOR_SERVICE ,
.Dv CAP_DOOR_ADMIN ,
.Dv CAP_DOOR_INFO ,
or
.Dv CAP_DOOR_SHM
right.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr door 3 ,
.Xr doorfs 4 ,
.Xr namefs 4 ,
.Xr capsicum 4
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
system call first appeared in this FreeBSD Doors implementation with ABI 12.
.Sh CAVEATS
The selector ABI is intended for the libdoor library
and may gain new selectors while retaining the existing ABI.
Use the public library unless implementing or testing the runtime itself.
